From: Spaced Linux Developers <dev@spacedlinux.com>
Subject: screenshot: start while Fire Writing or the zoom wheel holds a grab

The screenshot plug-in refuses to initiate while any screen grab other than
its own exists. Spaced binds Shift+Super+left-drag to Fire Writing and Shift+Super
to the zoom wheel, and both hold a screen grab for their shortcut
(firepaint.c: pushScreenGrab (s, None, "firepaint")), so Ctrl+Shift+left-drag
selects nothing while fire is being painted. The capture itself is safe over
another plug-in's grab: shotPaintScreen reads the composed framebuffer after
paintScreen, and the fire particles are drawn into that framebuffer by
firePaintOutput, so the fire is part of the image. Only a grab held by another
X client can break the selection, and that is not what otherScreenGrabExist
reports. Let the screenshot plug-in coexist with the two Spaced grabs.

--- a/plugins/screenshot.c
+++ b/plugins/screenshot.c
@@ -91,7 +91,12 @@
     {
 	SHOT_SCREEN (s);
 
-	if (otherScreenGrabExist (s, "screenshot", NULL))
+	/* Spaced: Fire Writing (firepaint) and the Spaced zoom wheel hold a
+	 * screen grab for their own shortcut. A screenshot must still work
+	 * over them: the image is read back from the composed framebuffer
+	 * (shotPaintScreen), so the fire is part of the picture. Only a grab
+	 * held by another X client can break the selection. */
+	if (otherScreenGrabExist (s, "screenshot", "firepaint", "ezoom-wheel", NULL))
 	    return FALSE;
 
 	if (!ss->grabIndex)
